ssion at once except an authentication failure, which records the failed call, releases only its lease and leaves the session record unchanged; and an occupancy percent at the dial (codex clamped to 85, FAMILY_RESET_CAP) drains it; a call's observation lands only while the route record still carries that call's own lease, a resumed call's only on the live session and generation it resumed, and landing drops that lease in the same whole-record write; a record another call took over, through its lease or a successor after stale-lease retirement, is left alone; when another call took that lease over, the call lands on nothing with reset reason store moved on whether that call still runs or has finished; the call's accounting gains session-gen and reset-reason. Bookkeeping never raises StoreBusy: when its apply is deferred, its accounting carries reset-reason pending and the call's own session-gen. A launch that raises retires the session it resumed (keep_abandon); a first mint that raises removes its lease-only record. This is guaranteed under lock contention for every marker kind: every locked read (load_honoured, in keep_for, keep_release, keep_bookkeep, keep_abandon, retire_scope and take_warm_lease) reads the clock first, then lists and folds the record's markers in publication order, then runs retire_stale_lease, so no reader retires a lease whose release was published before it observed expiry. A release drops its publisher's lease; a retire retires only the live session and generation it names and drops a lease only when its publisher holds it; a bookkeep lands under _landing's rule, and one that no longer lands releases its holder's lease if still held. Every marker therefore takes effect at most once: a call's marker only while its publisher's lease stands, and a scope retirement only on the live session and generation it names, so a marker left by a failed delete is inert on a later locked or lockless read. A lease-only record without a lease is removed. Each applied or spent marker is deleted by its own name, never another's; an unreadable marker stays and prevents expiry retirement on that read, while a malformed marker is deleted with one stderr line. The lockless readers (due_routes, _warm_candidates, scoped_route and _scoped_records) fold the same markers without deleting them: a pending bookkeep or release remains eligible for warm handling, while a pending retire is neither due nor pinned. KEEP-WARM (KeepWarmer, built by keep_warmer when keepwarm_minutes is also on, ticked once per dispatcher poll by run): keepwarm_due is true for an ANTHROPIC active session idle keepwarm_minutes while lanes are out, and a ping is taken only on a route whose runner's adapter bounds a call to one turn (claude's), so a route served through any other runner is never pinged; take_warm_lease prepares the selected route under the lock before any lease; a preparation refusal, or a prepared family differing from the record family, skips without a lease, otherwise the warmed Keep carries that Prepared family and home. The ping (role KEEP-WARM, source keep-warm, prompt ack, bounded by one_turn to --max-turns 1, a 300 s wall) runs on its own thread through act, so the tick never waits; one ping at a time, a due ping while one is in flight skipped and said; its session log is written and committed by the dispatcher's own thread between polls and only over a clean trunk, else held and said; at the run's end a ping in flight is waited out and recorded by the same rule, over a clean trunk only, and over a dirty one its log is not written and the reason is printed and returned. A ping whose launch raised TreeNotEnded hands it with the finished call to the dispatcher's thread, and the tick that sees it, or the run's end, raises it: over a clean trunk after recording the call, a failure to record riding as its context; over a dirty trunk unrecorded, the hold not deferring it. Any other failure of the ping is recorded as an ERROR call and the run continues. REVIEW. reviewer_dials is the one reader of the reviewer table: it reads a 0..100 non-boolean integer reset percent and persisted final reviewer only while that percent is positive; absent, unreadable, unparseable or ill-typed settings read as off and fresh. review_retention returns ReviewRetention(scope, stage, pin): it returns no scope for a non-review phase, no claim base, or an off review dial; a narrow round uses the iteration stage; a full round retires live iteration records through retire markers, which take effect for the lockless pin at once and are applied by the next locked read, and is unretained when fresh or uses the final stage when persisted. scoped_route pins a live record after folding its pending markers for the settled scope; unavailable pins fall through ordinary selection. Scoped records skip same-artifact reset, drain at the review percent, are clear at every round, and are never keep-warm due. _read_record is the one reader for load and scans: it accepts only writer-produced lease-only, retired-first, or full variants with all consumed fields typed and each optional occupancy, use or compaction field of its writer's type, filed under _record_name; any other object, absent or unreadable file is no record and the call mints. The loop stores scope, stage and once-resolved review template content in routing state, and passes scope and that content only for a review keep.\""," rationale = \"\"\"Retention is one more thing a call does, not a second launch path, so resume, occupancy, reset and keep-warm all go through act and record, and the rules and the store sit in their own module beside the service rather than in the roles. The layer ships off because turning it on is the owner's decision after it has been verified on the machine it runs on, and at the off dial the launch is exactly a fresh session's. The lock and the lease exist because a lane's worker and the dispatcher both reach the one store and the one transcript: a torn record or two calls resuming one session at once corrupts the state every later judgement reads. The clear point reads the queue and the lanes rather than the item alone because a draining session that retires while a successor of its own verdict is still queued breaks the round trip the layer exists for. The keep-warm ping is off the dispatcher's thread so a slow ping cannot stall the merges, and its record is on it so its commit is serialised with them. The dedicated homes keep a retained transcript out of a person's own sessions; a long-lived credential is read only for the launch that needs it, so no retained record becomes a credential store. The review class uses the existing store, lease and service homes rather than a copy; scoped identity keeps its records distinct from adjudicator records and preserves empty-scope filenames.\"\"\""," test_refs = \"(see TC-266, TC-267, TC-268, TC-322, TC-329, TC-330)\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-858\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3014,"oldLines":11,"newStart":3014,"newLines":11,"lines":[" [test.TC-267]"," verifies = [\"SR-227\", \"LLR-270\", \"IF-247\", \"IF-248\"]"," level = \"Unit\"","-method = \"With the dial on, over the recorded fixtures (all three LIVE: claude 2026-09-28, codex and opencode 2026-09-30), assert for each runner that the first adjudication mints (claude's pre-minted id, codex's thread id, opencode's session id recorded) with its occupancy and generation and releases its lease, and the next resumes by that id in the runner's own form, codex's without a working-directory or ephemeral flag. Drive a retained codex route and assert it launches under the dedicated CODEX_HOME created under the store, reading its occupancy from the rollout there, and that an unretained codex call reads occupancy under an inherited CODEX_HOME. Then one test per reset clause: under the dial the session stays active; cresting it drains without retiring; a draining session is still resumed while a queued adjudication succeeds an item it judged, while a lane is out on such an item, and for an item that continues its chain, and is retired at the first launch where none of these holds, the next launch minting generation 2; the chain is the transitive lineage, so a queued re-adjudication naming only the worker an adjudication sent back keeps the chain open, supersession links count, a cycle ends, and launching that re-adjudication continues the chain; a reported error, a non-zero exit and a timeout each retire at once; an authentication failure records the failed call, releases only its lease and leaves the session record unchanged, while another failure retires it; a launch that raises retires the session and releases its lease, and does so under a store lock another holder keeps throughout: the record is untouched while the lock is held, keep-warm skips it, and the next launch retires it and mints, leaving no tombstone; a changed agent guide, a changed loaded skill and a changed runner version each drain; the runner's version is read for a retained launch; the same-artifact guard retires before rejudging; the codex dial is clamped to 85; the loop folds the brief's template or its override into the governing inputs. For the store: no temporary or lock file is left after a write, a second holder of the store lock is refused, and an adjudication meeting a keep-warm lease runs unretained with the stated reason naming the holder; and when a holder's lease expires while it is still running, the next adjudication retires that session and mints rather than resuming it. Assert blackout retirement overrides a pending chain after the window, permits an in-window wrap-up resume, and suppresses keep-warm inside the window.\"","+method = \"With the dial on, over the recorded fixtures (all three LIVE: claude 2026-09-28, codex and opencode 2026-09-30), assert for each runner that the first adjudication mints (claude's p